{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-007-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/SceneExitFinalizationIntegrationTests.cs","line":3135,"method":"TryCompleteFinalizationFromPatchedSnapshot_NullSolver_VerboseRateLimitedPerRecordingAndReason","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/IncompleteBallisticSceneExitFinalizer.cs:550; drop {snapshot.FailureReason} from the rate-limit key -> green (test never fires a second failure reason); drop recordingId from the key -> red","what_it_asserts":"Five same-recording NullSolver snapshot failures within 0.5 s collapse to one VERBOSE and zero WARNs, and another recording's first NullSolver hit still emits.","why_weak":"The doc comment and name claim per-(recordingId, failureReason) rate-limiting, but every hit in the cell uses NullSolver; the reason segment of the key is unexercised. A non-NullSolver failure on the same recording inside the 30 s window would be silently suppressed by a key regression, and no cell catches that.","proposed_action":"After the 5-hit verbose floor, fire the same recording with FailureReason=MissingPatchBody inside the window and assert 1 WARN plus the NullSolver VERBOSE count unchanged; removing {snapshot.FailureReason} from the key then reds.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
